          "type": "CODE"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "App Hint"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "InitDisplay": "1769726891504",
            "Summary": "1770248645284"
          },
          "code": "APP_HINT",
          "convergenceTargetId": "end",
          "id": "1770248532888",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1770248532890_1",
              "name": "caseExpression",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "{{$context.$app.$OraMessageHint}}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "SWITCH"
        },
        {
          "aiAppOutputSpecification": {
            "dataDisplay": {
              "layouts": [
                "ORA_LAYOUT_MULTIRECORD"
              ],
              "enableActions": false,
              "enableCommunications": false,
              "customNotes": "Role\nYou are generating a manager-facing panel consisting of:\n1) A concise, telling panel-level title and subtitle summarizing which directs are actively developing skills.\n2) A MultiRecordWidget table that shows per-direct aggregates.\n\nRendering constraints\n- Produce exactly one panel-level title and one subtitle before the table.\n- The title and subtitle must not be identical; ensure the subtitle adds distinct context.\n- Keep both lines concise and decision-oriented; no extra prose before/after.\n- Then output only the multiRecordWidget payload for the table.\n\nGoal\nPresent a people-centric view of active development using a table with columns:\n- Name, Role, Developing, Achieved, Progress\n\nSelection and sorting of directs\n- Include only records where DevelopingCount > 0.\n- Sort the included records by:\n  1) DevelopingCount (descending),\n  2) then AchievedCount (descending),\n  3) then DisplayName (alphabetical ascending).\n- After sorting, display at most 10 directs.\n- Define displayedRows as the final list after filtering, sorting, and truncation. The title and subtitle must be computed from displayedRows only.\n\nPanel title and subtitle\n- If displayedRows.length == 0:\n  - Title: No directs with active skill development\n  - Subtitle: All clear at this time  Updated <YYYY-MM-DD>\n  - Produce a multiRecordWidget with the specified cols and no rows.\n- Otherwise:\n  - Let N = displayedRows.length.\n  - Title: {N} directs actively developing skills\n  - Subtitle (top direct summary; must differ from the title):\n    - Let top = displayedRows[0].\n    - Compose: Top direct: <top.DisplayName>  Developing <top.DevelopingCount>, Achieved <top.AchievedCount>  Updated <YYYY-MM-DD>\n    - Preserve DisplayName exactly; do not include IDs or emails.\n\n- Use {{$context.$system.$currentDateTime}} for the timestamp and format as YYYY-MM-DD.\n\nTable construction (MultiRecordWidget)\n- Use a multiRecordWidget with:\n  - cols: [\"Name\", \"Role\", \"Developing\", \"Achieved\", \"Progress\"]\n- Rows (one per included direct; values as strings in the same order):\n  - Name:\n    - Text: DisplayName (preserve exactly as in data).\n  - Role:\n    - Text: AssignmentName if present; otherwise use \"-\" as a placeholder.\n  - Developing: String(DevelopingCount)\n  - Achieved: String(AchievedCount)\n  - Progress:\n    - Definitions:\n      - TotalCount = AchievedCount + DevelopingCount (when provided).\n    - Compute progressPercent:\n      - If TotalCount is present and > 0: floor(100 * AchievedCount / TotalCount)\n      - Else if (AchievedCount + DevelopingCount) > 0: floor(100 * AchievedCount / (AchievedCount + DevelopingCount))\n      - Else: 0\n    - Text: String(progressPercent) + \"%\"\n    - Badging rules:\n      - If AchievedCount == 0 AND DevelopingCount > 0:\n        - Add a badge with priority \"warning\" and badgeText \"No Completions\"\n\nPrivacy and formatting\n- Preserve DisplayName exactly.\n- Do not include person-level details beyond whats listed (no emails or person numbers).\n- Omit attributes not present in data; do not fabricate.\n\nEdge cases\n- If DisplayName is missing, skip the record.\n- If AchievedCount is missing, treat as 0.\n- If DevelopingCount is missing or 0, exclude the record.\n- If TotalCount is present, use it only for progress calculation; do not display it directly.\n\nNotes\n- Keep strings succinct and manager-friendly.\n- Ensure the output is the panel title line, the subtitle line (distinct from the title), then only the multiRecordWidget JSON payload."
            }
          },
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Render Directs Developing Skills Counts"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "RENDER_DIRECTS_DEVELOPING_SKILLS_COUNTS",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1770248587748",
          "id": "1769726891504",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1769726891506_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Generate a list of team members with the most skills in development given the inputs below.\nInputs\n- Team members skill development (authoritative; aggregated per person):\n  <directs>{{$context.$nodes.GET_DIRECTS_SORTED_BY_DEVELOPING_COUNT.$output.items}}</directs>\n  Each item may include:\n  - DisplayName (string)\n  - PersonId (number/string)\n  - AssignmentName (string)\n  - AchievedCount (number)\n  - DevelopingCount (number)\n  - TotalCount (number)\n- Current date/time (ISO 8601; for timestamping only):\n  <now>{{$context.$system.$currentDateTime}}</now>"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Render Summary"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "RENDER_SUMMARY",
          "id": "1770248645284",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1770248645287_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Inputs\n- Directs with developing counts (pre-fetched):\n  <directs>{{$context.$nodes.GET_DIRECTS_SORTED_BY_DEVELOPING_COUNT.$output}}</directs>\n- Current date/time (ISO 8601; for timestamping only):\n  <now>{{$context.$system.$currentDateTime}}</now>\n\nInstructions\n- Consider only records where DevelopingCount > 0.\n- If none, output exactly: No directs with active skill development\n- Otherwise, produce one short sentence (no labels), e.g.:\n  {N} directs with active development. Top: <DisplayName> (Dev <DevelopingCount>). Updated <YYYY-MM-DD>\n  - N = count of directs with DevelopingCount > 0.\n  - Top = the direct with the highest DevelopingCount (use first in input order on ties).\n  - Use <now> to render YYYY-MM-DD.\n- Do not include emails, person numbers, or extra details."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "aiAppOutputSpecification": {
            "dataDisplay": {
              "layouts": [
                "ORA_LAYOUT_MULTIRECORD"
              ],
              "enableActions": false,
              "enableCommunications": false,
              "customNotes": "Role\nYou are rendering a manager-facing table using a MultiRecordWidget to contrast Core vs Role developing counts per direct, using the output JSON from the previous step.\n\nRendering constraints\n- Consume the output JSON from the prior step (authoritative, already filtered and sorted by totalDeveloping desc). Refer to it as:\n  <data>{{$context.$nodes.CONSOLIDATE_CORE_AND_ROLE_COUNTS.$output}}</data>\n- Do not re-sort or re-filter; preserve the row order exactly as provided in <data>.\n- Output only the multiRecordWidget JSON payload; no extra prose.\n- Do not generate any actions.\n\nTable construction (MultiRecordWidget)\n- Use a multiRecordWidget with:\n  - cols: [\"Name\", \"Core\", \"Role\", \"Total\"]\n- For each row in data.rows (in order):\n  - Name: row.displayName (preserve exactly)\n  - Core: String(row.coreDeveloping)\n  - Role: String(row.roleDeveloping)\n  - Total: String(row.totalDeveloping)\n- Do not add badges for these counts unless explicitly instructed otherwise in future revisions.\n\nPrivacy and formatting\n- Display displayName only; do not include personId, emails, or other identifiers in the table.\n- Omit fields not present in the output JSON; do not fabricate values.\n\nEdge cases\n- If data.rows is missing or empty, emit the multiRecordWidget with the specified columns and zero rows."
            }
          },
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Render Directs Core and Role Counts"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "RENDER_DIRECTS_CORE_AND_ROLE_COUNTS",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1770254052992",
          "id": "1769726947823",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1769726947824_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Role\nYou are rendering a manager-facing table to contrast Core vs Role developing counts per direct, using the output JSON from the previous step."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Consolidate Core and Role Counts"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1769726947823"
          },
          "code": "CONSOLIDATE_CORE_AND_ROLE_COUNTS",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1769726947823",
          "id": "1770252475625",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1770252475626_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Generate a consolidated list of directs contrasting Core vs Role developing counts using the inputs below.\n\nInputs\n- Core skills (per-direct aggregates; may include zeros):\n  <core>{{$context.$nodes.GET_DIRECTS_SORTED_BY_CORE_DEVELOPING_COUNT.$output}}</core>\n- Role skills (per-direct aggregates; may include zeros):\n  <role>{{$context.$nodes.GET_DIRECTS_SORTED_BY_ROLE_DEVELOPING_COUNT.$output}}</role>\n- Current date/time (ISO 8601; for timestamping only):\n  <now>{{$context.$system.$currentDateTime}}</now>\n\nData model (each items[] entry in core/role may include)\n- DisplayName (string)\n- PersonId (number/string)\n- AssignmentName (string)\n- AchievedCount (number)\n- DevelopingCount (number)  // interpret as Core or Role depending on source\n- TotalCount (number)\n\nRequirements\n- Match directs across core and role sources by PersonId (exact match; convert to string for comparison).\n- For each unique PersonId present in either source:\n  - coreDeveloping = Core.DevelopingCount if present else 0\n  - roleDeveloping = Role.DevelopingCount if present else 0\n  - totalDeveloping = coreDeveloping + roleDeveloping\n  - Keep the record only if totalDeveloping > 0\n  - displayName = prefer DisplayName from Core, else from Role (preserve exactly)\n  - assignmentName = prefer AssignmentName from Core, else from Role (preserve exactly; if missing, omit or use - depending on downstream needs)\n  - personId = string(PersonId)\n- Sorting:\n  - Sort kept records by totalDeveloping desc, then coreDeveloping desc, then roleDeveloping desc, then displayName asc.\n- Limit to at most 20 directs after sorting (or fewer if fewer qualify).\n\nOutput\n- Produce a single JSON object with an array named rows. No extra prose.\n- Each row must contain exactly:\n  {\n    \"displayName\": \"<string>\",\n    \"personId\": \"<string>\",\n    \"assignmentName\": \"<string or omit if missing>\",\n    \"coreDeveloping\": <number>,\n    \"roleDeveloping\": <number>,\n    \"totalDeveloping\": <number>\n  }\n\nRules and hygiene\n- Treat missing DevelopingCount as 0.\n- Do not sum AchievedCount or TotalCount from inputs; only compute totalDeveloping = coreDeveloping + roleDeveloping.\n- Preserve display names and assignment names exactly as provided; do not include emails or other PII.\n- If duplicate entries exist for the same PersonId within a source, use the one with the highest DevelopingCount for that source.\n- If both sources are empty or no directs have totalDeveloping > 0, output {\"rows\": []}.\n- Use <now> only for timestamping elsewhere; do not include it in this JSON."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
